# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Every file in this repository is authored with LF endings, and the SHA-256
# values recorded in PACKAGE_MANIFEST.md were computed over LF content.
# Without these rules, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows materializes the working
# tree as CRLF on checkout, and every recomputed hash would differ from the
# import receipt. These rules keep checkouts byte-stable across platforms so
# integrity verification stays meaningful.
#
# Recorded under Directive 0.1, section A.5 (finding F-08).

# Conservative default: let Git decide what is text, and normalize it in the
# repository. Binary files are left untouched.
* text=auto

# Explicit LF for all authored text formats.
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell stays CRLF: some Windows PowerShell hosts are sensitive to LF-only
# script files.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
